---
/* ============================================================
   LeadIn — sets the opening words of a piece in small caps, the
   magazine way into an essay.

     <LeadIn>I’m on stage, palms damp, holding my script.</LeadIn> As I …

   Wrap a phrase or the first sentence you choose, rather than styling
   "the first line": where a line breaks changes with screen width, so
   a first-line rule stops mid-sentence at a different word on every
   device. Newsreader (as self-hosted) has no true small caps, so the
   browser synthesizes them; keep the lead-in to a sentence at most.
   ============================================================ */
---

<span class="lead-in"><slot /></span>

<style>
  .lead-in {
    font-variant-caps: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-small-caps);
  }
</style>
